      \field{abstract}{Over recent years, second-home tourism has gained special relevance, leading to the publication of numerous works that attempt to analyze this type of tourism from distinct perspectives. This has resulted in a trend within the scientific literature that deals with analyzing the economic impacts of this tourism. Although different systematic reviews have been performed, taking different approaches, no review of the scientific literature has undertaken the analysis of the main economic impacts generated by second-home tourism. This study presents a comprehensive review of 33 peer-reviewed papers. The impacts seem to be positive on employment, especially in sectors such as construction and property maintenance, or on spending and economic growth by favoring retail activity, but negative on rental and housing prices. Therefore, policy recommendations include the application of retail incentives, the granting of licences for holiday home rentals or the application of tax incentives, among others.}
