      \field{abstract}{The rise of short-term rentals (STRs), particularly through platforms like Airbnb, has significantly influenced real estate markets, sparking widespread academic and social debate. While extensive research has focused on urban contexts, studies on traditional coastal tourist destinations remain limited. This research examines the case of Calpe, a sun-and-beach tourist destination on the Spanish Mediterranean coastline. Using time series analysis techniques for the period 2010–2024, the relationship between STRs, rental prices, and property sales is explored. Findings indicate that STR proliferation typically correlates with higher housing prices and rental prices. However, after incorporating relevant control variables an inverse relationship is revealed for the case of rental prices. The study underscores the need for localized regulatory approaches to mitigate STR impacts and balance tourism’s economic benefits with social sustainability. These insights offer critical guidance for policymakers addressing housing challenges in established tourist destinations.}
